  <layout>One block of italic Latin verse, in stanzas, with some small-capital words in roman. Running head top left, page number top right. Signature at the bottom right. No marginal notes.</layout>
  <page_number>53</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIACA</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>D. iij.[?]</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Sic tanto ille magis crudior extitit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Quanto frena magis laxa cupidini</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Tractauit, nimia capta licentia.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4" para="true">
      <i>At vt forte bonus montibus aduolat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Pastor, qui validi pectoris[?] &amp; manus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Robur munierit follicitudine</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Dilecti pecoris: tum grauis irruit:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Crudelemque ferum conficit, &amp; nece</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Vna, seruat oues quæ reliquæ manent:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10" para="true">
      <i>Sic tu, summe Deus, qui vigil intuens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Vastantem miserè septa gregis tui</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Amanum, subito robore comprimens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Sistis, ne solitis sæuiat artibus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14" para="true">
      <i>Infandúsq; cadit ter merita nece,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Multos immeritos qui dederat neci:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Multisq; immeritam concilians necem.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Sic seruas, &amp; oues, ô Bone, vindica-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>s.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19" para="true">PASTOR adest DEVS.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">
      <i>Pastori ergo Deo pangite carmina:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Samson Christus adest. En catulus perit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Vastator, fugiunt agmina Gazica.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23" para="true">
      <i>Dauid Christus adest: millia millium</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Vnus dum Goliath occidit, occidunt.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25" para="true">
      <i>Ergo continuis vocibus accinam,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Quotquot sancta Dei numina diligunt,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Quotquot sancta Dei robora prædicant,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Quotquot facta Dei ter bona connotant.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29" para="true">
      <i>Cernis continuis fœdus ut Imbribus</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Verse is italic throughout; small-capital words (PASTOR, DEVS) are set in roman. "Pectoris" is the least certain reading of the damaged line 'pe_oris', copied from the scan with a [?]. Signature "D. iij." read from a small, faint mark; the numeral could be "ij" and is marked [?]. Show-through from the facing page appears on the right side and is left out.</notes>
</page>
